					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-393947#post-1265604</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-393947/interval-2#post-1265604</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 23 Sep 2011 20:24:27 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Salman Corbette</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>678987</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>As an answer to A, this is a very circles-within-circles type of site, where mind screws are the norm and subtlety is expected. We pride ourselves in adding twists to stories and putting in little extras for the reader to decipher. The response to this article actually made me smile, since there was a bunch of people trying to figure out the hidden message or the greater implications.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-393947#post-1265598</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-393947/interval-2#post-1265598</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 23 Sep 2011 20:17:32 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>thedeadlymoose</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>732274</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <blockquote> <p>What is it with kids trying to write stories explaining old in jokes they don't actually know the explanations for? I'm blaming thedeadlymoose and his black moon bullshit for this one. Downvoted.</p> </blockquote> <p>A) To me, it's clear that this isn't supposed to be an explanation, but rather a joke. No one's saying Mr. Sillybug's an actual Little Mister just because Interval 1 is about Mr. Sillybug. I can see that a couple others took it as an explanation as well, but I don't personally understand why. (Someone care to pipe up? I'm sure Salmander would like to know.)</p> <p>B) The black moon thing I wrote was absolutely terrible and I should have known better. It also existed for&#8230; maybe thirty minutes. That's quite the influential thirty minutes there, yo. :P</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
